@startuml fr12-reminders
' Origin: drafted with AI assistance (Claude Code) from FR-12 in docs/02-requirements.md; reviewed by the author.
title FR-12 Contextual goal reminders (stream processing trigger)
|Focus streams|
|Planner|
|Student|
|Focus streams|
start
split
  :Consume DistractionLogged (focus.distractions);
  :Group by userId, 30-minute tumbling windows\naligned to the clock (event time = loggedAt);
  :Count distractions (distraction-spike-store);
  if (count = 3 exactly?) then (yes)
    :Publish **DistractionSpikeDetected** → focus.alerts\n(once per window);
    |Planner|
    :Consume DistractionSpikeDetected;
    if (reminder for this window exists?\n(triggerKey spike:<windowStart>)) then (yes)
      :Ignore duplicate;
      stop
    else (no)
      :Create DISTRACTION_SPIKE reminder;
    endif
  else (no)
    |Focus streams|
    :Nothing;
    stop
  endif
split again
  |Planner|
  :MissedBlockScheduler runs every minute;
  :Find blocks still PLANNED whose end has passed;
  :Mark each MISSED;
  :Create one MISSED_BLOCK reminder per block\n(triggerKey missed:<blockId>);
end split
|Planner|
if (student has not-achieved goals or values?) then (yes)
  :Quote one at random in the message;
else (no)
  :General encouragement + tip to add a goal;
endif
|Student|
:GET /reminders (unread, newest first);
:POST /reminders/{id}/read;
|Planner|
if (already read?) then (yes)
  :409;
else (no)
  :Record readAt;
endif
stop
@enduml
